## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical concurrency patterns: dedup across concurrent requests, bounded queues, and cache integration in a real-world service.

## Key Concepts

- Per-key deduplication (singleflight)
- Bounded queues and backpressure
- Cache coherence and eviction
- Failure handling and retries

## Code Example

```javascript
const inflight = new Map();
async function fetchFlag(key){
  if (inflight.has(key)) return inflight.get(key);
  const p = remoteFetch(key).finally(()=>inflight.delete(key));
  inflight.set(key,p);
  return p;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle remote fetch failures?
- How would you extend to support priority keys or TTL-based eviction?

